A||||5||ChopTop||Crank sensor on 4 cyclinder ?||||1||
Z||000000||ChopTop||11-02-2001||09:31 AM||||Folks is there a crank sensor on the 88 4 cylinder?  And if there is and it is cracked would it leak omhs?   <BR>Sorry for my ingnorance but right now my mechanic is telling me he believes the reason I'm having stalling problems is I have a bad ignition module and on further inspection he noticed a crack crank sensor, 27 bucks for replacement.  Does this make sense???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-02-2001||09:55 AM||||The crank sensor on the 87 & 88 2.5s is located under the ignition module and coils. If it is cracked it can give all sorts of headaches including rough and uneven idle, stalling, poor fuel economy due to bad timing etc..<BR>Go ahead and replace it and check the module, it should be OK.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChopTop||11-02-2001||10:24 AM||||Thanks IRG.  When he first told me I was like huh?  Never heard anyone talk about a crank sensor on the forum.  Especially one that leaks OHMs(?) if it's cracked.  Thanks for the feedback.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-02-2001||12:09 PM||||Well it doesn't leak ohms( that a line of bull) it's a magnetic pickup ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||11-02-2001||12:40 PM||||I doubt that the ignition module is bad, unless it has been subjected to an immense amount of heat, i.e. the coils had been serviced and the heat sink compound was not replaced like it should have been.<P>A new CPS cost me $15 at autozone, the case was all cracked.  As for leaking ohms, impossible, and even if he was referring to a sensor that actually had resistance as a reading I would still give the guy a funny look if he said to me "it's leaking ohms"<P>Also, if you want to put a new one in yourself I can help ya if you run into a problem, Ive had the coil pack and all that apart on my 87 before.  you can call me if you want, 719 7649<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-02-2001||08:06 PM||||The info you need is pretty much all in my cave article. DIS notes in the engine menu.<P>If the crank position sensor is damaged replace it BEFORE replaceing the ignition module. You may still need the module but the $20 CPS is allot cheaper of a test.<P>Notes in that article also tell you which bolts need thread sealer.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
